ria-docs: Plan for PR: - add "Streaming and split JSON" note under structured output - include SDK snippets (Python + TS) and an opt-in API `assemble_stream` / `assembleStream` - add server guidance + migration checklist (server-side escaping, array shape, content-type header) - include netcat repro and QA tests - bump SDK recommendation to v1.12.1 and call out this helper in migration notes. Tagging @devin-sdk and @pat-qa for review.

jon-ml: Also include an observability/telemetry blurb: we'll emit a `stream_parse_fallback` metric for the next release so customers can see if their tool outputs triggered the issue.

ria-docs: Quick docs wording note: make it explicit that the helper is a mitigation for malformed streams and not a substitute for correct output formatting on servers. Keep examples short and prefer the array-of-lines pattern where producers control serialization.

devin-sdk: Agree. I'll add unit tests for split-chunk cases and add an example integration that runs the netcat repro in CI-only job.

pat-qa: I'll add the test vectors to the docs PR so maintainers can click "run examples" in the preview.

